const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"联合报告记录2010年5月6日市场事件，并梳理当日价格、成交与市场结构条件之间的关系。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“Findings Regarding the Market Events of May 6, 2010” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://www.sec.gov/files/marketevents-report.pdf",label:{zh:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · 来源说明",en:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"这是监管调查报告，围绕特定事件窗口整合跨市场交易与报价证据，而非一般化的资产定价回归。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “Findings Regarding the Market Events of May 6, 2010”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://www.sec.gov/files/marketevents-report.pdf",label:{zh:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · 来源说明",en:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"阅读需保留事件时钟、交易场所、合约与股票身份、订单和报价字段，以及数据覆盖差异。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “Findings Regarding the Market Events of May 6, 2010”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://www.sec.gov/files/marketevents-report.pdf",label:{zh:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · 来源说明",en:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"报告的价值在于重建极端时段的市场过程；它不提供一个可脱离该事件的普遍因果公式。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “Findings Regarding the Market Events of May 6, 2010”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://www.sec.gov/files/marketevents-report.pdf",label:{zh:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · 来源说明",en:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"核对所有时间戳的时区、跨市场同步方式、取消与更正记录，以及报告版本所覆盖的证据范围。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “Findings Regarding the Market Events of May 6, 2010”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://www.sec.gov/files/marketevents-report.pdf",label:{zh:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · 来源说明",en:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 SEC / CFTC joint report (2010)。单次压力事件不能代表平常流动性，也不能据此推断任一市场的日常执行质量。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) for “Findings Regarding the Market Events of May 6, 2010”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://www.sec.gov/files/marketevents-report.pdf",label:{zh:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · 来源说明",en:"SEC / CFTC joint report (2010) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“Findings Regarding the Market Events of May 6, 2010”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。单次压力事件不能代表平常流动性，也不能据此推断任一市场的日常执行质量。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “Findings Regarding the Market Events of May 6, 2010”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
